# Files in this directory that are not the app (PLAN 17.16.2).
#
# `wrangler.jsonc` uploads everything under `web/` as a static asset, so
# without this the host would serve the README, the deploy config and the
# drift-checking script alongside the pages. None of them is a secret — this
# repository is public and `config.js` is *meant* to be served — but a deploy
# should publish the app and not its scaffolding.
#
# If Wrangler ever stops honouring this file the failure is visible rather than
# silent: `curl <host>/README.md` answers with the file instead of a 404.
README.md
check-deployed.sh
config.example.js
wrangler.jsonc
.assetsignore
